  "narrative": "Combo F Recovery dominates at week 10 of MEDIUM duration, driven by NFCI at -0.506 (39th percentile over 3 years), signaling continued financial conditions normalization that supports the bullish equity outlook. This combo's 79% 6-month hit rate and +5.5% average return override the competing bearish signals from confirmed Combo E legs, as Recovery patterns historically outperform during Fed cutting cycles with steepening curves.\n\nCombo F Recovery remains ACTIVE since April 3rd with 79% 6-month hit rate, reflecting financial conditions stabilization as NFCI holds at -0.506, well above crisis levels that would invalidate the recovery thesis. Combo E Valuation Extreme shows CONFIRMED status with CAPE and NFCI legs active, posting 19% 12-month hit rate with CAPE at 42.7 (99th percentile) marking severe overvaluation, while NFCI confirms the financial conditions component. Combo B Capitulation holds WATCH status with no current signal activation, monitoring for potential capitulation conditions that could trigger tactical shifts.\n\nRecovery dominates for three reasons: (1) NFCI at -0.506 sits in normal territory rather than the sub-1.0 readings that historically derail recoveries, indicating financial stress remains contained despite regional war tensions; (2) the CUTTING_LATE Fed cycle with STEEPENING curve regime creates optimal conditions for risk asset appreciation, as rate cuts provide liquidity while curve steepening signals growth expectations; (3) GLOBAL_EASY liquidity conditions with HY spreads at 2.8 (17th percentile) demonstrate credit markets pricing continued expansion rather than recession risk.\n\nThe closest historical analog remains June 2019, when Fed pivot expectations during trade war tensions created similar recovery dynamics, delivering +4.2% 3-month, +8.1% 6-month, and +12.8% 12-month SPX returns. March 2016 provides secondary comparison during Fed pause with energy stress, yielding +6.3% 3-month, +11.2% 6-month, and +15.8% 12-month returns. October 2011 offers tertiary match during European crisis resolution, generating +7.8% 3-month, +14.1% 6-month, and +18.9% 12-month gains.\n\nSystem maintains TACTICAL_EASY_MONEY posture based on Recovery dominance and supportive regime factors. Posture shifts require: (1) NFCI deterioration below -1.0 for three consecutive weeks, indicating financial stress escalation; (2) CFTC positioning reversal above -200,000 contracts, signaling speculative excess return; (3) VIX sustained above 30 for five trading days, confirming fear regime activation that would override recovery dynamics.",
